<section class="how" aria-label="How reet.sh works">
 <article><span>01</span><h2>Enrol a machine with one command.</h2><p>Run the agent on a laptop, a VPS or a lab box. It dials out to your controller, so there is no port to open, and reports in with the agents, skills and setups it already has.</p></article>
 <article><span>02</span><h2>Agents, skills and setups stay in sync.</h2><p>Push a skill to one machine or to all of them, bring back what you find, and review every change before it applies. A new machine ends up with the same reet good toolkit as the rest.</p></article>
 <article><span>03</span><h2>Put your agents to work.</h2><p>Open a browser terminal to use the agents installed on any enrolled machine, keep sessions running, and pick up where you left off.</p></article>
</section>
